00:16:46,728 --> 00:16:46,968
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

302
00:16:47,288 --> 00:16:48,408
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, yeah.

303
00:16:48,448 --> 00:16:49,848
[SPEAKER_02]: I've hit them on purpose, too.

304
00:16:50,289 --> 00:16:50,729
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, you have?

305
00:16:50,769 --> 00:16:52,109
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't think bitches did that.

306
00:16:52,429 --> 00:16:52,969
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, yeah.

307
00:16:55,854 --> 00:16:58,255
[SPEAKER_02]: I had an example in Pittsburgh one day.

308
00:16:58,795 --> 00:17:01,277
[SPEAKER_02]: Red Smith, he was a catcher with the Giants.

309
00:17:02,337 --> 00:17:04,278
[SPEAKER_02]: Some way, McGraw hated him.

310
00:17:05,099 --> 00:17:05,739
[SPEAKER_02]: Didn't like him.

311
00:17:06,899 --> 00:17:08,520
[SPEAKER_02]: So he traded him to Pittsburgh.

312
00:17:09,541 --> 00:17:11,502
[SPEAKER_02]: Now, we're playing in Pittsburgh next year.

313
00:17:12,902 --> 00:17:16,544
[SPEAKER_02]: And I got a man on second base and a man on third base.

314
00:17:17,625 --> 00:17:18,585
[SPEAKER_02]: And I got two men out.

315
00:17:20,906 --> 00:17:22,187
[SPEAKER_02]: And Red Smith is a hitter.

316
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:23,188
[SPEAKER_02]: He's a left-hand hitter.

317
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:24,148
[SPEAKER_02]: He's a pretty good hitter.

318
00:17:25,773 --> 00:17:30,937
[SPEAKER_02]: And so I was a knuckleball pitcher, see.

319
00:17:30,957 --> 00:17:33,480
[SPEAKER_02]: He fouled two knuckleballs off on me.

320
00:17:34,540 --> 00:17:36,262
[SPEAKER_02]: He had two and nothing on him, see.

321
00:17:37,943 --> 00:17:52,095
[SPEAKER_02]: So when I got two strikes and no balls on him, McGraw was over on the bench, jumped up on the front row of a dugout, and hollered at me.

322
00:17:53,477 --> 00:17:53,957
[SPEAKER_02]: He said,

323
00:17:54,562 --> 00:18:00,004
[SPEAKER_02]: If this one is anywhere near that plate, he said, it's going to cost you $500.

324
00:18:00,104 --> 00:18:04,086
[SPEAKER_02]: I want to see this guy hit the dirt.

325
00:18:05,006 --> 00:18:07,227
[SPEAKER_01]: Did Smith hear this?

326
00:18:08,447 --> 00:18:09,248
[SPEAKER_01]: Everybody could hear this?

327
00:18:09,348 --> 00:18:12,949
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh yeah, the umpires, they'd have to just stand there.

328
00:18:13,049 --> 00:18:18,651
[SPEAKER_02]: I used to walk up, oh within six feet of the hitter, and say, get ready, you're going down.

329
00:18:20,732 --> 00:18:22,553
[SPEAKER_02]: And turn around and walk back.

330
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:29,544
[SPEAKER_02]: So when I finished this other, my girl said, now you remember this.

331
00:18:30,585 --> 00:18:36,329
[SPEAKER_02]: So he had a sign with the catcher, from the bench to the catcher.

332
00:18:36,849 --> 00:18:43,735
[SPEAKER_02]: And the catcher kept looking in at him, kept looking in at him, and no signs.

333
00:18:44,255 --> 00:18:51,120
[SPEAKER_02]: He just standing there, making a lot of neck red and the face red, but no knockdown signs.

334
00:18:55,808 --> 00:19:04,190
[SPEAKER_02]: Finally, Red Smith backed up out of the batter's box and stood there and looked at McGraw and stood there.

335
00:19:04,490 --> 00:19:09,451
[SPEAKER_02]: Finally, he got back up in there and the catcher went down and gave me a fastball sign.

336
00:19:10,111 --> 00:19:11,112
[SPEAKER_02]: But no knockdown.

337
00:19:11,132 --> 00:19:13,032
[SPEAKER_02]: See, that was our knockdown.

338
00:19:13,972 --> 00:19:16,513
[SPEAKER_02]: So he didn't give me that, he just gave me a fastball sign.

339
00:19:17,533 --> 00:19:19,934
[SPEAKER_02]: So I wound up and I threw one right down the middle.

340
00:19:21,873 --> 00:19:27,375
[SPEAKER_02]: Smith had the bat up here, and he started back, and he started falling backwards on his heels, you see.

341
00:19:27,495 --> 00:19:33,337
[SPEAKER_02]: And they're firing us in the corner, third strike, and the game's over.

342
00:19:33,377 --> 00:19:39,979
[SPEAKER_02]: So we had to go through the Pittsburgh dugouts and get to the clubhouse in the old Pittsburgh park.

343
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:48,582
[SPEAKER_02]: And he stood there at the top of the deck of the dugout, and he said, well,

344
00:19:49,972 --> 00:19:52,755
[SPEAKER_02]: He said, I wanted to give a nickel for my chances then.

345
00:19:54,216 --> 00:19:57,919
[SPEAKER_02]: I said, I just took a chance.

346
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:03,023
[SPEAKER_02]: He thought he was going to get knocked down with all the drug talking.

347
00:20:03,704 --> 00:20:05,225
[SPEAKER_02]: So the game's over.

348
00:20:05,485 --> 00:20:07,327
[SPEAKER_02]: So McGaugh runs off of the bench.

349
00:20:08,008 --> 00:20:08,548
[SPEAKER_02]: Runs out.

350
00:20:08,728 --> 00:20:10,029
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm just walking off.

351
00:20:10,109 --> 00:20:12,211
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm not going to run off.

352
00:20:12,231 --> 00:20:14,613
[SPEAKER_02]: He runs out to the mound.

353
00:20:15,033 --> 00:20:16,074
[SPEAKER_02]: He said, listen to me.

354
00:20:16,094 --> 00:20:18,036
[SPEAKER_02]: He said, I'll strike those hitters out for you.

355
00:20:19,825 --> 00:20:23,588
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, he was just really intimidating Smith.

356
00:20:23,648 --> 00:20:26,971
[SPEAKER_01]: Making him defeat twice.

357
00:20:27,611 --> 00:20:28,712
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, defeat a minute.

358
00:20:29,173 --> 00:20:35,838
[SPEAKER_02]: You see, he'd get whatever sign he used with the catcher, his fist, or whatever it was, to knock him down.

359
00:20:37,079 --> 00:20:38,540
[SPEAKER_01]: But giving no sign.

360
00:20:38,580 --> 00:20:39,661
[SPEAKER_02]: No sign.

361
00:20:41,162 --> 00:20:44,164
[SPEAKER_02]: So the catcher was smart enough, he'd just give me a fastball sign.

362
00:20:44,705 --> 00:20:47,347
[SPEAKER_02]: And I don't say I was smart enough,

363
00:20:47,792 --> 00:20:56,838
[SPEAKER_02]: But I just wound up, I said, well, hell, I didn't see a knockdown pitch, so I'm just going to grab back and throw as hard as I can right down the middle.

364
00:20:57,439 --> 00:20:58,239
[SPEAKER_02]: See if he takes it.

365
00:20:58,459 --> 00:20:59,060
[SPEAKER_02]: And he did.

366
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:08,646
[SPEAKER_02]: And I was, I've been, I've got no, everybody's telling me, would you rather be playing now than then?

367
00:21:08,747 --> 00:21:09,607
[SPEAKER_02]: I said, I don't know.

368
00:21:09,707 --> 00:21:14,831
[SPEAKER_02]: I said, of course, I'd have made a lot more money than I make now.

369
00:21:14,851 --> 00:21:15,131
[SPEAKER_02]: See?

370
00:21:15,451 --> 00:21:16,572
[SPEAKER_02]: I held out one year.

371
00:21:18,991 --> 00:21:22,092
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the year I won the pennant.

372
00:21:22,152 --> 00:21:24,713
[SPEAKER_02]: Not won the pennant, but led the National 30?

373
00:21:25,373 --> 00:21:28,013
[SPEAKER_02]: No, no, in 28 when I had that.

374
00:21:28,874 --> 00:21:31,774
[SPEAKER_02]: And I held out.

375
00:21:31,934 --> 00:21:33,615
[SPEAKER_02]: McGraw made me hold out.

376
00:21:33,635 --> 00:21:41,917
[SPEAKER_02]: See, he was the vice president of the ball club, and he called me in the office after the season was over, the last game, and said, now, he said, I'll tell you something.

377
00:21:42,717 --> 00:21:45,378
[SPEAKER_02]: I want you to get a raise now.

378
00:21:45,938 --> 00:21:47,038
[SPEAKER_02]: I said, don't you sign.

379
00:21:47,951 --> 00:22:05,679
[SPEAKER_02]: So McGraw goes to Cuba every winter and doesn't report to San Antonio until the regulars get there, the catchers and outfielders and infielders.

380
00:22:05,939 --> 00:22:13,743
[SPEAKER_02]: But the pitchers are there about ten days so they can get ready to pitch batting practice by the time everybody else gets ready and start the ballgames, you see.

381
00:22:14,123 --> 00:22:16,764
[SPEAKER_02]: So McGraw comes when the regulars come.

382
00:22:17,823 --> 00:22:23,189
[SPEAKER_02]: And I'm two weeks late, and they issued an order out of New York.

383
00:22:23,289 --> 00:22:31,998
[SPEAKER_02]: It was $100 a day fine that anybody holding out didn't report on.

384
00:22:32,038 --> 00:22:35,582
[SPEAKER_02]: $1,400 fines.

385
00:22:36,403 --> 00:22:38,225
[SPEAKER_02]: So McGraw got into San Antonio.

386
00:22:38,265 --> 00:22:40,167
[SPEAKER_02]: He saw what he called me.

387
00:22:41,985 --> 00:22:43,565
[SPEAKER_02]: He said, what's the matter?

388
00:22:43,826 --> 00:22:45,406
[SPEAKER_02]: And I said, you know what's the matter?

389
00:22:45,466 --> 00:22:47,907
[SPEAKER_02]: You told me to stay here if I didn't get a raise.

390
00:22:48,667 --> 00:22:50,628
[SPEAKER_02]: And they didn't give me a raise.

391
00:22:52,048 --> 00:22:55,749
[SPEAKER_02]: And he said, well, he said, you just hang on now.

392
00:22:55,769 --> 00:22:58,750
[SPEAKER_02]: He said, you get on the first plane you can.

393
00:22:59,250 --> 00:23:00,191
[SPEAKER_02]: Come on down here.

394
00:23:01,111 --> 00:23:02,451
[SPEAKER_02]: So I got on the plane.

395
00:23:02,511 --> 00:23:06,873
[SPEAKER_02]: And when I got down there, he had me all straightened out a little fine.

396
00:23:07,233 --> 00:23:07,753
[SPEAKER_01]: Got the raise?

397
00:23:07,773 --> 00:23:08,893
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, I got a little raise.

398
00:23:12,998 --> 00:23:14,020
[SPEAKER_02]: I got a $2,500 raise.

399
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:18,926
[SPEAKER_02]: Now, if you'd win that, now you'd ask for a $40,000 or $50,000 raise.

400
00:23:24,428 --> 00:23:26,749
[SPEAKER_01]: Eddie Roush was with me a few years ago.

401
00:23:26,769 --> 00:23:29,671
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, he was with Cincinnati and then he came over to the Giants.

402
00:23:29,691 --> 00:23:31,052
[SPEAKER_01]: He didn't stay there very long.

403
00:23:31,092 --> 00:23:32,513
[SPEAKER_01]: He liked to hold out, didn't he?

404
00:23:32,733 --> 00:23:34,754
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh yeah, he didn't believe in spring training.

405
00:23:34,774 --> 00:23:35,975
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the only thing about him.

406
00:23:36,035 --> 00:23:38,096
[SPEAKER_02]: It wasn't the holding out that meant anything.

407
00:23:38,336 --> 00:23:41,618
[SPEAKER_02]: He didn't believe in going to spring training and using all that.

